    "extract": "More Songs About Buildings and Food is the second studio album by the American rock band Talking Heads, released on July 14, 1978, by Sire Records. It was the band's first of three consecutive albums produced by Brian Eno, and saw the band move toward an increasingly danceable style, crossing singer David Byrne's unusual delivery with new emphasis on the rhythm section of bassist Tina Weymouth and drummer Chris Frantz.",
